WWP IT RUNBOOK RB-05 - BACKUP AND RESTORE
Owner: Kevin Tran                                  Rev. 2026-05-18
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

WHAT IS BACKED UP
  ww-fs01   /srv/samba (all shares)    nightly 23:00 to backup appliance,
                                       30 daily / 12 monthly
  ww-it01   /etc config tarball        nightly via cron script
            /opt/it-scripts/nightly_config_backup.sh ->
            /var/backups/it/<host>-etc-YYYY-MM-DD.tar.gz  (14 days kept)
  ww-web01  site content + DB          nightly 01:00
  OT systems  Engineering's responsibility (PLC project backups on ww-eng01)

THE CONFIG BACKUP SCRIPT (ww-it01)
  - Lives in /opt/it-scripts/ so the helpdesk can maintain the include list
    without needing root (group "helpdesk" has write access to the folder).
  - Runs as root from /etc/cron.d/it-config-backup.
  - Log: /var/log/it-config-backup.log

RESTORE A FILE FROM THE CONFIG BACKUP
  sudo tar -tzf /var/backups/it/ww-it01-etc-2026-05-17.tar.gz | grep ssh
  sudo tar -xzf /var/backups/it/ww-it01-etc-2026-05-17.tar.gz -C /tmp/restore etc/ssh/sshd_config

RESTORE FROM THE BACKUP APPLIANCE
  Open a ticket; Kevin or Dana run the restore from the appliance console.
  Test restores are done quarterly (last: 2026-04-09, OK).
